+# S004 Data Model
+
+## Existing concepts to locate
+
+The workspace has no source code. The implementation must extend the host application's existing workspace quota and reminder-send attempt records rather than replace them.
+
+## Entities
+
+### Workspace retry quota
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `workspace_id` | Owning workspace | Primary ownership scope. |
+| `available_retry_credits` | Credits available to begin an attempt | Integer greater than or equal to zero. |
+| `updated_at` | Last quota mutation | Updated in the same transaction as a reservation mutation. |
+
+### Reminder send attempt
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `attempt_id` | Stable id for one provider send attempt | Unique and immutable. |
+| `workspace_id` | Owning workspace | Must match the reservation workspace. |
+| `provider_delivery_id` | Provider correlation id, if returned | Maps callbacks to the known attempt; not a replacement for `attempt_id`. |
+
+### Retry credit reservation
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `reservation_id` | Durable reservation identity | Primary key. |
+| `workspace_id` | Quota owner | Must match the referenced attempt and quota. |
+| `attempt_id` | Attempt consuming this credit | Unique per workspace; permits reserve replay without a second debit. |
+| `state` | `pending`, `finalized`, or `released` | Terminal states are immutable. |
+| `release_reason` | `provider_failed`, `timed_out`, `cancelled`, or `rolled_back` | Required only for `released`. |
+| `created_at` / `settled_at` | Lifecycle timestamps | `settled_at` required for terminal state. |
+
+## Relationships
+
+```text
+Workspace retry quota 1 ─── * Retry credit reservation * ─── 1 Reminder send attempt
+```
+
+## State transitions and invariants
+
+| From | Event | To | Atomic balance effect |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| none | reserve(`attempt_id`) with positive balance | `pending` | decrement one credit and create/reuse reservation |
+| `pending` | provider accepted | `finalized` | none |
+| `pending` | provider failure, timeout, cancellation, or rollback | `released` | increment one credit |
+| `finalized` or `released` | duplicate terminal callback | unchanged | none |
+
+- `available_retry_credits >= 0` always.
+- A reservation may produce at most one debit and at most one compensating credit.
+- A reservation may be settled only from `pending`.
+- The quota mutation and reservation mutation share one transaction.
+- Replaying `reserve` for the same workspace and attempt returns the existing reservation without another debit.
